plugin-qualify (0.21.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: plugin-qualify 0.21.3 (0.21.2 to 0.21.3), a patch
  * release-matrix: the deb target is arm64 alone, as plugin-hostd's debs are
    (#196)
  * build.sh packs before it links the packaged omx-contract
  * The package bundles the channel's omx-contract, not the registry's, as
    the wave builds it
  * release: a devel push's install check reads the staging channel its build
    was staged to
  * contract: the contract directory has no schema-major level
  * domains: every domain is at 0.1.0, its vocabulary own version, never the
    package one
  * release.yml: the installed job judges each kind's skipped build on its own
  * release: a devel merge that built nothing skips the install checks
  * release: a merge to devel publishes the real package to staging
  * packaging: no version on the organisation's own packages
  * domains and descriptors: no floor on a domain, and no requires in a
    scanned descriptor
  * qualification domain: judged by its words, never by its info.version
  * ci.yml: a pull request into devel may take its packages from the staging
    channel
  * .githooks/commit-msg is the shared stub, byte for byte
  * measurement: the sweep reader lands cost and memory (format 1.7)
  * readProbeOutput: probe output format 2, the cost unit nsPerSample is
    required
  * tests: probe output format 2, the cost unit is nsPerSample (red first)
  * test: QUALIFICATION_REASON_PARAM_WORDS holds every step the adapter can
    name (#169)
  * qualify-spool: only an isolation that holds may start a check (lint green)
  * plugin-qualify-sync --plugin <target> [--under-load]: one plugin, never a
    scan
  * qualify domain 1.1.0: QUALIFY_RUN_CONDITIONS, the word measured-under-load
  * test: plugin-qualify-sync --plugin gives one plugin a record, a pin and a
    descriptor, and --under-load keeps its figures out of the store (red)
  * fixtures: the Pi's records live only under records-rpi5
  * make docs-site and docs.yml: the commands' man pages and guide published
    per release under /reference/plugin-qualify/ (Open-Mixer/.github#242)
  * records-package: the provenance names its cell in grid, as the store
    reads it
  * test: a records package names its cell in the provenance's grid (red)
  * records: a record names its binary below the install root wherever it is
    written
  * test: a record --out writes names its binary below the install root (red)
  * qualify-sync: name every plugin the machine left unmeasured
  * test: a sync names every plugin the machine left unmeasured (red)
  * qualify-sync test: the lock tests order two runs by the lock, not a 300
    ms sleep
  * workflows, Containerfile: Node 26 everywhere
  * test: every workflow and the Containerfile ask for Node 26 (red)
  * store-export: the store writer's Python is named in its own repository
  * ci: describe's oracle is built and run in the Fedora 45 container job
  * tests: describe's oracle is built where the channel serves the loader
    (red)
  * packaging: the probe domain floor is plugin-hostd-protocol-contract 0.8.0
  * tests: the probe domain floor is plugin-hostd-protocol-contract 0.8.0
    (red)
  * probe words: the probe domain is plugin-hostd-protocol's; the packages
    floor its contract package
  * tests: the probe domain is plugin-hostd-protocol's, the packages floor
    its contract package (red)
  * signal sites: the sweep reader and the crash table read the probe
    domain's signal words
  * tests: the signal sites test carries the sweep reader's full row (red)
  * tests: the sweep reader and the crash table name signals with the probe
    domain's words (red)
  * build-native: say what the omx-clap-core-contract floor is
  * probe words: the judging code reads the outcome and signal words from the
    probe domain
  * describe: the scopes of a field dump are the scan domain's words
  * tests: describe takes the scopes of a field dump from the scan domain
    (red)
  * Floor plugin-hostd-contract at 0.21.0, pin the exact domain (sorting
    pass, V5)
  * The qualification domain is plugin-hostd's: this package reads it from
    the installed place (sorting pass, V5)
  * tests: the judging code compares a probe's output with the probe domain's
    words (red)
  * Test, red first: the qualification domain is plugin-hostd's, read from
    the installed place (sorting pass, V5)
  * the qualify runner's probe end has its own name, clear of the records'
    (R-112)
  * the qualify runner: a spool request is qualified isolated and always gets
    a verdict (R-112)
  * tests: the qualify runner's rule, before the runner (R-112)
  * plugin-qualify: the Pi's records are a plain fixture, and the upgrade
    scriptlets no longer refresh pins
  * commit-msg: the shared stub without the old FREEMIXER names
  * plugin-qualify --version answers as its sibling tools do (#72)
  * record-figures: the citation of a Python twin goes; the fork reads
    figures through plugin-db
  * test: a tool or test a source cites exists (red)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:54:56 +0000
